# Build context exclusions, shared by Dockerfile.etl and Dockerfile.backend.
#
# Two reasons this file matters more than usual here:
#   1. `az acr build` TARBALLS AND UPLOADS the whole context to Azure before it
#      builds. Without these rules that upload includes frontend/node_modules
#      and ~12 MB of Parquet, which is slow on every single deploy.
#   2. .env holds a live storage connection string. A stray `COPY . .` in a
#      future edit would bake that secret into a published image layer, where
#      it stays readable forever via `docker history`. Excluding it here means
#      the secret is not even in the context to be copied by accident.

# --- secrets: never in a build context ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- the lakehouse itself ----------------------------------------------
# Data is regenerated by the job, never shipped inside the image.
data/

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.prefect/

# --- Node / frontend ----------------------------------------------------
# Neither image serves the dashboard: it deploys to Vercel as static files.
frontend/
node_modules/

# --- VCS, editors, CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- docs and tests -----------------------------------------------------
# Excluded to keep the layer small; tests run in CI against the source tree,
# not inside the shipped image.
docs/
tests/
*.md

# --- container assets (a Dockerfile never needs to be inside its own image) --
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
